thin each group. Changes of settings, methods or step sizes do not add independent physical problems. Cold-plasma oscillation with electrostatic CIC PIC Couple electrons to a 1D periodic grid by CIC, solving Poisson and particle motion self-consistently. Assumptions, units and boundaries Dimensionless length 2pi, electron charge/mass −1, stationary ion density one and plasma frequency one. A quiet start receives a small sinusoidal displacement of amplitude 0.001. Adopted numerical method Combine CIC deposition and matching field gathering, a mean-zero spectral Poisson solve and velocity Verlet. Set the field Nyquist mode to zero for a real skew-adjoint spectral derivative. x˙i=vi,v˙i=−Eh(xi),−ϕxx=ρ,E=−ϕxx˙i​=vi​,v˙i​=−Eh​(xi​),−ϕxx​=ρ,E=−ϕx​ A(t)/A(0)≃cos⁡(ωpt),ωp=1A(t)/A(0)≃cos(ωp​t),ωp​=1 References and measured quantities Separate a 32/64/128-grid sweep from timestep refinement on a 512 grid. Compare displacement amplitude with continuum linear cos(t), and check charge compatibility, potential-Poisson residual and single-particle self force. Verification limits and failures Finite amplitude and finite particles leave an error floor. Nonlinear instabilities, Landau damping, collisions, electromagnetic/relativistic PIC and open particle boundaries are unvalidated. Stored measurements and decisions Display values are rounded. Acceptance uses original fixed-input tolerances and unrounded numbers; only stored results passing every check are presented. 量 / metricMeasured value mode_error0.000886723736396 time_mode_error0.000438557578256 charge_error1.743934249e-16 poisson_residual1.05879118407e-22 self_force3.33066907388e-16 grid_refinement_ratio0.057532353094 time_refinement_ratio0.0142609763205 判定 / checkPassed mode_errortrue charge_errortrue poisson_residualtrue self_forcetrue time_errortrue grid_refinestrue time_refinestrue Figure from saved results. See the text and JSON for input, reference and acceptance scope.Read every stored record seriesgriddtparticleserrore